A||||22||87GTZ34||David Letterman's stupid Fiero tricks||||3||
Z||000000||87GTZ34||05-01-2001||10:40 PM||||No it doesn't rollover or anything.  But I was at the drive-thru pharmacy buying... well nevermind about that.  Anyway, it was night & I had the lights on so I wanted to put my park lights on.  For some reason I put my index finger on the off switch and the 'one next to it' on the park light switch and hit them in succession with no lag time.  To my surprise, the headlights went off but they stayed flipped up.  I thought that would be a good thing to do when washing the car by hand.  Anyone else have any unusal 'tricks' performed by their car?||||reg||3
Z||000001||fiero56||05-01-2001||10:50 PM||||I always just pull the h/d switch out with the tip of my finger.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierofreek2001||05-01-2001||11:10 PM||||my parking lights have to be on while doing that tho.. is your cars the same?<BR>steve||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bob Englert||05-01-2001||11:31 PM||||I have wired up a toggle switch that I mount on the back gauge cover panel behind the headlight switch.  I use a small flat toggle switch from radio shack.  <P>The instructions on how to do this are in the N.I.F.E. web site at <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-controlpopups.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-controlpopups.html</A> <P>Makes it real easy to leave the headlights up when running into the store at night for a moment or if the weather is very cold.  I believe it will save a lot of cycles of the headlight motors.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||05-01-2001||11:41 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87GTZ34:<BR><B>To my surprise, the headlights went off but they stayed flipped up.  I thought that would be a good thing to do when washing the car by hand.  Anyone else have any unusal 'tricks' performed by their car?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>heheh mine does the same thing.. Kinda cool little trick If I hold the button down or push it down at anytime the lights will lower...<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||05-02-2001||12:08 AM||||That is how you are suppose to clean the hidden headlights. It's the same as the Firebirds. The Firebird owners manuals tell you how to do it. HMMM I'll have to look at my 86 Owners manual to see if they noted it in there.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierodave2001||05-02-2001||01:16 AM||||Here's another trick,<P>I have an 87 GT, AM/FM/CASS/EQ/w/Subwoofer<P>The trick is, if you push the low & high volume control at the same time, the sound goes to full volume instantly ! In a split sec.<P>I did this one day, and scared the heck out of me. I almost drove off the road.<P>(I've heard this happens only w/the EQ system ?)<BR>||||reg||10
