Z||000020||Ken Wittlief||05-03-2001||03:34 PM||||Okay here is a real fiero trick I havent heard anyone mention. I discovered if you short the A and B pins on the test connector (same ones you use to get the codes, and to set the timing) and you start the car up, it will tell you if the ECM is running in closed loop or open loop mode.<P>  if the temp sensor is bad it will think it is always cold and will not switch over to closed loop mode after a few minutes like its suppose to.<P>   If it is running open loop it blinks 3 times a second, if its running closed loop it blinks once a second<P>   and the really cool part is, if the mixture is correct the blinks are 50% on and 50% off. if its running rich its on more than its off, if its lean then its off more than its on (short flashes).<P>  I havent heard anyone mention this yet. Its a great way to trouble shoot you EMC, gives you a better idea of whats going on.<P>  found the info inthe Chilton manual, no wait, Clymer?! One of those, i forget which.||||reg||1
Z||000021||84Bill||05-04-2001||12:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>Okay here is a real fiero trick I havent heard anyone mention. I discovered if you short the A and B pins on the test connector (same ones you use to get the codes, and to set the timing) and you start the car up, it will tell you if the ECM is running in closed loop or open loop mode.<P>  if the temp sensor is bad it will think it is always cold and will not switch over to closed loop mode after a few minutes like its suppose to.<P>   If it is running open loop it blinks 3 times a second, if its running closed loop it blinks once a second<P>   and the really cool part is, if the mixture is correct the blinks are 50% on and 50% off. if its running rich its on more than its off, if its lean then its off more than its on (short flashes).<P>  I havent heard anyone mention this yet. Its a great way to trouble shoot you EMC, gives you a better idea of whats going on.<P>  found the info inthe Chilton manual, no wait, Clymer?! One of those, i forget which.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>DAMNIT JIM I"M A DOCTOR NOT A SCIENTIST<P>||||reg||1
